# No Em Dashes In User-Facing Copy

Do not use the U+2014 em dash character anywhere in user-facing website, application, documentation, translation, onboarding, error, notification, or marketing copy.

This rule exists to keep product copy clean, readable, consistent, and aligned with the required writing style.

## Applies To

This rule applies to strings and content shown to users, including:

- UI copy
- Page copy
- Button labels
- Form labels
- Error messages
- Empty states
- Loading states
- Toast messages
- Modal content
- Tooltips
- Onboarding content
- Dashboard text
- Help text
- Policy text
- Legal references
- Report text
- Markdown content rendered in the app
- Translation files
- Localization files
- Seed data displayed in the UI
- Static content files
- Generated user-facing documents

Common file locations include:

- `src/i18n/**`
- `src/messages/**`
- `src/locales/**`
- `src/content/**`
- `src/data/**`
- `src/components/**`
- `src/pages/**`
- `app/**`
- `components/**`
- `content/**`
- `data/**`
- `public/**`

## Preferred Replacements

| Writing Intent | Use Instead |
|---|---|
| Title plus subtitle | Colon |
| Parenthetical clarification | Parentheses |
| Contrast or correction | Period, comma, or conjunction |
| Label plus detail | Colon |
| Citation plus title | Colon |
| Interruption or emphasis | Rewrite as two clean sentences |
| Long explanatory sentence | Split into shorter sentences |

## Replacement Examples

```text
Incorrect:
Connect With Support [U+2014] No Details Required

Correct:
Connect With Support: No Details Required